# Follow-up to -29.play, same cell (mode=battleground map=flags
# spec=druid:restoration style=auto view=844x390,touch save=carried). The
# first run showed every heal slot on the action bar reading "range" by
# fightTime~64s (healing_touch/rejuvenation/swiftmend/starsurge all "range",
# only the self-buff barkskin "ready") while the player stood still under
# AUTO, then died around fightTime~83s and was still hp=0/locked five seconds
# later when the chained play() calls were cut short by playbot's own
# abort-on-hero()===null quirk. This run plays to the same death, then uses
# bare wait/state polling instead of chained play (the "Tried and dropped"
# lesson) to get a clean read on the respawn, and continues on to the match's
# actual end (Ebb and Flow's real limit is 180s per #278).
open
tap battleground
tap map:flags
tap class:druid:restoration
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
state

play auto 90
shot a1
state
bill

wait 15
state
shot a2

wait 15
state
shot a3

play auto 90
shot a4
state
bill
says
targets
